why={'clink': 'Native launch(a) directly invokes lstm_inference for each three cases between steady_clock start and sync/elapsed. Julia clink_study creates factory-returned closures for three input/weight cases; timed repeat invokes f() then device synchronization. KA factory explicitly binds kernel handle and JACC explicitly binds function kernel; no name-only callback inference. Initial CuArray setup, warmup, oracle/readback outside. Scientific scope fixed LSTM inference operator, not trained-network quality.', 'clock': 'Selected native lambda invokes timedReduction; percase reset before start,100 repeats then synchronized elapsed. Actual Julia overlay main names clock_reduction! callback and includes actual overlay common; complete executed overlay text is retained in frozen plan and hash checked. Common timed100loop invokes supplied callback; reset/fill and guard/rawclock capture outside. Source output is Float32 minimum plus64bit hardware clock observations; comparison/clock ops are not ordinary add/mul/FMA work. Native historical main dormant; sampled invocation remains unknown.', 'cobahh': 'Native run(S) resets seven state arrays and flag guards, then invokes cobahh for case steps within timer before synchronized elapsed. Included neurongroup_stateupdater host wrapper is not called by selected study main. Julia study(allocate,launch) passes actual launch callback to run(c), which loops launch after start and before sync/elapsed; KA explicit named kernel instantiation and JACC explicit neuron_kernel! function. Three selected cases have1/1/3 frozenclock iterations, not full progressing-clock physiological simulation. Reset and oracle/guards outside.', 'collision': 'Native launch(Case) invokes both warp duplicateflag and duplicatemask kernels;100repeats after source start and before device sync. Julia supplied closure runs collision_flags! and collision_masks!, explicit KA instances/JACC callbacks, from shared timed100loop. Reset flags/mask precedes start; complete input echo/oracle/guards after elapsed. Source integer warp shuffle/vote control; no scalarFP operator implied. Native renamed original main dormant.', 'colorwheel': 'Native study includes renamed legacy_main, warms color once and repeats same color kernel between source t0/sync/elapsed. Julia study_prepare closure explicitly binds color_kernel!/portable_color!; shared study_main calls study_loop!(launch!,repeats) inside timer; fill/reset, oracle and readback outside. CUDAjl strips trailing exit(main()) before defining callback. Float32 angular/color arithmetic/SFU and UInt8 conversion remain source semantics, not inferred hardware precision. Same function warmup stage regex disabled separately.', 'compute-score': 'Native launch invokes integer compute then reduction, and is repeated between steady_clock start and sync/elapsed; renamed original main dormant. CUDAjl study strips legacy exit(main()), factory returns explicit two CUDA calls; KA/JACC equivalent factories bind actual kernels. Shared score_study passes factory closure to OwnedStudy.run_trials! timed launch loop; score/high/low resets and independent checks/readback outside. Integer/bitpacked score arithmetic not ordinary scalarFP work.', 'contract': 'Native each trial resets output/guards, calls contraction once as warmup BEFORE start, then ten contraction launches followed by device completion and elapsed. Original included main renamed/uninvoked. Julia contract_study factory closure explicitly binds contraction! (KA namedhandle,JACCfunction); run() before start is warmup, ten run() calls inside timer. STUDY_DTYPE branch is selected from actual environment/default and retains Float32/Float64 scope,18 tensor cases; oracle/guards/readback outside.', 'conversion': 'Native run<D,S> guards/setup/input copy and one cvt warmup precede start; ten cvt calls inside timer then sync/elapsed, full bitpattern oracle/readback afterwards. Source-selected dtype pair dispatch in main visits fixturecases. Julia study constructs source/destination types from six-entry TYPES tuple BF16/FP16/FP32/Int32/Int8/UInt8, run(c) invokes explicit convert_kernel! via callback ten times between start/sync/elapsed. Guard fills/warmup/oracle outside; conversion instructions are not ordinary add/mul/FMA counts. Original undefined-input main renamed/uninvoked; scientific contract qualification unchanged.', 'convolution1D': 'Native launch_typed loops mode0:2 and blockwidth64:1024, binding conv1d/basic,tiled,tiledcaching; launch dtype dispatch covers Float64/Float32/Int16. Timed three repeats invoke launch after prepare(maskcopy/outputreset) and before synchronization. Julia study_main iterates24groups and15mode/blockwidth paths, dispatching Val mode1 basic/else tiled; KA explicit two kernels, JACC conv_jacc! with source Val mode and spec/template dictionary. Maskcopy/reset/oracle outside timed group; initial warmup same kernels. CUDAjl legacy main PROGRAM_FILE guard false for study.jl. No family count inferred from aliases or compiled specializations.', 'convolution3D': 'Native run(style) chooses explicit conv3d_s1/s2/s3 and study main visits all3styles within perstyle ten-repeat synchronized timer, with outputreset outside. Julia study passes run! closure and visits styles1:3; CUDAjl source ternary selects actual conv3d_s1/2/3_kernel!, KA/JACC pass Val(STYLE) into conv_body with corresponding grid permutation. Callback source map is explicit, not inference from grid() helper name. Shared mathematical operator spans3layout mappings; no fullCNN/physicalvolume claim. Oracle/readback/warmup outside; native legacy_main renamed/dormant.'}
